  "body": "Found in the review read of PR #3599 (#3525).\n\n**Now:** the depth in the `flute_short` note and warning is measured from the top of the raw setup stock (or the part top when there is no stock).\n\n**Example:** a Face operation clears 30 mm below the raw top. Then a 2D Pocket cuts 3 mm deep with a tool that has a 20 mm flute. The note says \"cuts 33.000 mm below the stock top\" on a clean path.\n\n**Effect:** the finding is advisory and never holds the post. The text can mislead.\n\n**Wanted:**\n- Measure the depth against the material that remains at the cut, or\n- say \"below the raw stock top\" and do not state that the shank goes into the cut when no body finding exists.\n- Also: the warning text says that the findings after it name the moves where the shank meets material. Those findings can also be `RapidInStock` or `Gouge`. Correct the sentence.\n- Also: the texts are in mm in an inch document.\n\n**Done when:** a test with a faced stock and a shallow pocket gets no misleading depth.\n",
